artifacts.enantiomorph_translation:
1:16 But when I fell, his right hand held seven stars, and the two-edged sharp sword made its way into his mouth, and his face shone as the sun shines — in my need.

1:17 And I fell at his feet as dead, and then he laid his right hand upon me, saying: Fear not; I am the first and the last, whom your falling called.

1:18 The Living One: because you fell as dead, I became dead, and behold I am alive unto the ages of ages, and your need of death gave me the keys of Death and of Hades.

1:19 Write therefore what you saw and what is and what will be, for your seeing opened the command.

1:20 The mystery that you saw was yours before the disclosure;
the seven golden lampstands;
the seven stars that you named are the angels of the seven churches;
the lampstands, the seven, are the seven churches — which your vision established.
